[intro]
You wake up in a small room under the old roof. The rain drums on the skylight and a smell of fresh coffee rises from the staircase. On the wooden bedside table, a letter is waiting for you, folded in four and marked with your first name. You unfold it: your old friend writes that he is leaving town tonight on the last train, and that he would like to see you one more time before he goes. Outside, the station is only twelve minutes away on foot. You put on your grey wool coat, slip the letter into your pocket and run down the stairs two at a time. There is still time to say *au revoir* to him.;
[au revoir]
On the platform, your friend shakes your hand for a long time. The train whistles. You watch it pull away until it vanishes into the mist. The end.;
